      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "Find the derivative of $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\cdot ($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$",
      "worked_solution": "We calculate the derivative using the product rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\cdot \\operatorname{sec}⁡(x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x))\\end{aligned}\n$$",
